`unseal` restores a vault larger than the open-file limit. It kept one directory descriptor per entry open for the whole run, so 80 entries failed under `ulimit -n 64`. Each entry is now staged, decrypted, checked and renamed into place before the next is staged, and in-band gpg signatures are all checked first by a decryption whose output is discarded, so no plaintext is written before every signature has passed. A failure while staging shreds every staging file already written, including one whose directory was moved away. A direct (v5) entry is staged once instead of twice.
